  "grade": "artifacts:audit-end-states",
  "description": "session.disconnect closes a session's audit record and says how it ended and why (session model §12–§13; Storage §6's table; decision 5.45). end_state killed is an end by TSB or through it: end_reason idle, unattended or orphan (the session model §11 timers, which have no actor, so no user) or owner or admin (the principal who ended it, named in user). end_state terminated is an end from outside TSB: end_reason worker_lost (its worker died, hung, or was not where its manifest said), target_closed (the target closed its SSH channel or the connection) or connection_lost (our end of the connection is gone, or link_timeout fired). A reason from the other state's list is refused, as are the retired reasons grace and lifetime and the retired state disconnected, and there is no expiry event: a timer's end is killed. The session's recording ends in the end marker of the same end_state (C8 end-marker-killed). A collected run must hold at least one end event, and no session may end twice; a worker death's is graded from e1 (C8 worker-death-recorded).",
  "corpus": [
    "Storage §6",
    "session model §11",
    "session model §12",
    "session model §13",
    "decision 5.44",
    "decision 5.45",
    "immortality §1.1"
  ],
